# One line-ending standard for the whole repository.
#
# Without this file, normalization depends on each contributor's local
# `core.autocrlf`, which is a per-machine setting — so the repo has no opinion
# and CRLF leaks into the index from whichever machine has it off. That is what
# produced the "read the file's existing line ending and write it back the same
# way" workaround that used to live in CONTEXT-MEMORY.md. Delete the cause, not
# the symptom.
#
# `eol=lf` applies to the WORKING TREE as well as the index, deliberately: the
# checkout then matches what is committed, on every platform, so there is no
# per-file line ending to discover before writing to it. Every tool in this
# stack (node, pnpm, vite, git bash) is fine with LF on Windows.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts break outright with CRLF, including inside the Docker image.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf

# Never touched.
*.png  binary
*.svg  text eol=lf
*.ico  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf  binary
